Index: openwiki/.claims/flows/ca-bootstrap.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/flows/ca-bootstrap.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/flows/ca-bootstrap.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:5ffa1d8fb8088d6b1f622c53eb7e7a02c9f4d3d786c4956cdbbf2fddc6cfbcd0",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ceaf8416a6874e898398f7a01e1a7dcd",
+      "statement": "bootstrapAction selects between team and direct bootstrap: --team with --ca-url or --fingerprint is rejected; --team plus --team-authority calls BootstrapTeamAuthority(team, teamAuthority); --team alone calls it with the default authority sub-domain \"ssh\"; --team-authority without --team errors; otherwise --ca-url and --fingerprint are both required and BootstrapAuthority runs.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/bootstrap.go#L85-L111",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9233088e1d6b59adda81887d92d0e867322f64b15dddaffc7f86ff7f8b6fc0fa:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b6ff67c356c843d18795a75533107260",
+      "statement": "BootstrapTeamAuthority queries https://api.smallstep.com/v1/teams/<team>/authorities/<teamAuthority> by default, or a --team-url endpoint with <> placeholders replaced by the team ID, using an unauthenticated HTTP GET that maps 404 to 'authority not found'.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L226-L246",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d1037f5b3440f80aa67d275baecce4e132bc0d5529de0f046e39eacecf7f2a9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c2e461f79ee24bf3b228484026097f0f",
+      "statement": "The team endpoint returns {url, fingerprint, redirect-url, provisioner, min-password-length}; a CLI --redirect-url overrides the API value, otherwise https://smallstep.com/app/teams/sso/success is used when both are empty, and the default context name is <teamAuthority>.<team>.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L273-L293",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca59ebb4b5c2fdf539d37a888d3afd438932160ed8de63f06f712e5aa62b6cb3:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L28-L34",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e9151c85fc80b36be8da663e772ab26f619f2ec3b6ba4a7834933f00118f004:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e77ab8837c274237b354dff54d75f82b",
+      "statement": "BootstrapAuthority derives the default context name from the --authority flag or the CA URL hostname with the port stripped via getHost, and passes any --redirect-url through to bootstrap.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L296-L317",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:89d6290a779ebdfffcf4ea8629c188763649c1dde065dd070ba0585a67870f19:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_bfc658ecb40c403daf4f1458de441f50",
+      "statement": "The bootstrap routine creates the CA client with ca.WithInsecure() and calls client.Root(fingerprint); the client validates that the returned root matches the SHA-256 fingerprint, which is the trust-pinning mechanism shared with step ca root.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/root.go#L86-L91",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:157aeb1301772a99b7db7acd3f9cf327645e6243e4f1e8c5794896829eb3930f:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L104-L113",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:939535ef6f951facbf7472eaeeffa3804afc1a98ec9ba220fbdfdeafb198c170:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b207bbb046694f8f81b9fb7901d8b0f1",
+      "statement": "bootstrap participates in contexts when UseContext holds, adding the context, saving it as current, and activating it; otherwise it warns about contexts when $STEPPATH/config/ca.json exists.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L115-L144",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ec88be2faab9a1fa16dc4ee1592e594831bd683a4452ab7bacb0bbfb077bcae:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_76aa977935974a8cb0909ca6b712e919",
+      "statement": "bootstrap creates the root's parent directory with mode 0700 and serializes the downloaded root certificate to pki.GetRootCAPath() with file mode 0600.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L145-L165",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e086b853c6bb99d41699c79197a46fb606007800256026caba656d12a3ec71f6:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0463df3af10d4983bd60dc854088be09",
+      "statement": "bootstrap normalizes the CA URL with utils.CompleteURL (defaulting the scheme to https), writes defaults.json (mode 0644) with ca-url, fingerprint, root, and optional redirect-url/provisioner/min-password-length, and sets ca-url/fingerprint/root into the live CLI context.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L163-L195",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c8dad2704d2937afe1c07bd871cb502a570587a7adacbc2278660941f822b7e4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_25a2b9ebca5b4a13b961fd9e812ef13f",
+      "statement": "With contexts enabled, bootstrap seeds the profile defaults file (step.ProfileDefaultsFile()) with {} when it does not exist.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L197-L210",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd0525574d4d23a4ef560e8abf9b7cf01e1ddc6e34a15cd970ce491d66391510:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_80c0ed44b76e49b4867ca6250d3980bd",
+      "statement": "With --install, bootstrap installs the downloaded root certificate into the system trust store via truststore.InstallFile.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L212-L219",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5a81d2fc87277a3168775f5640a4ddaadc53d1cfcf809778b4c57f7f4a0e116:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f6acfe8ac1ad466ab752b8c7ab3f91d7",
+      "statement": "step ca root requires a fingerprint, downloads and validates the root via client.Root, and either writes it to the given file with mode 0600 or prints the PEM to stdout.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/root.go#L86-L108",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd010570fcc6f538af8cb54b2d95880b222781cc4b79dd5f10d03dcba99dce58:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9fc91e01e005414e9f551bf23a295e4e",
+      "statement": "step ca roots and step ca federation fetch the root bundle and federation bundle from the CA through the same client's Roots() and Federation() calls.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/federation.go#L114-L154",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac4ad3dd3963977fd262b5caa03edd11de53276a1672b0f103af2587396fb7f5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-08-31T08:02:07.014Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/flows/x509-certificate-issuance.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/flows/x509-certificate-issuance.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/flows/x509-certificate-issuance.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:05b3afab64f70b1cb21d446208ae4ca34d95e491458f46fe61ca848ab6167b30",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3549510944af4f6584e48a1254404125",
+      "statement": "step ca certificate takes a subject, certificate file, and key file; it requires 3 positional arguments unless --attestation-uri is set, rejects --offline combined with --token, and rejects --attestation-uri combined with --kms.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/certificate.go#L220-L244",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c01acc092e392b839d490c1001d564a7a189af177e6a15a656851bf162e29562:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d82fa4952e2f44a08515ac7d54d8d3ab",
+      "statement": "Without --token, an explicit --acme provider goes directly to the ACME flow; otherwise flow.GenerateToken runs the shared token flow, and an ACMETokenError from a selected ACME provisioner transparently switches the command to that provisioner's ACME flow.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/certificate.go#L250-L267",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c751b96694e00f8e2b1c15f9d20d460f1bff4fd671c6991ba880d8ed7813783f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_abd0b8adb2d34b62bce7421f4c93ed13",
+      "statement": "CreateSignRequest parses the token insecurely, generates the key from kty/curve/size, and builds the CSR from the token type: AWS/GCP/Azure derive default SANs from the instance identity document unless custom SANs are disabled, OIDC uses the token subject/email plus iss#sub URI, and K8sSA takes the subject from the command line.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L297-L405",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe53899bde3bce36ab21793922c426824f2a4864808cc9c7d2c810ac5d3b3c55:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ea8bc92015db41e7b8c7b19661fc0ec8",
+      "statement": "For JWK tokens the CLI rejects --san together with an explicit --token and requires the positional subject to equal the CSR common name; for OIDC/AWS/GCP/Azure/K8sSA the common name is validated server-side.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/certificate.go#L280-L303",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28848163c708b169cb3dc616578f0d08fcafdf55b2a6eaf704b7509482fccae1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e7cf2c1252404824a7bda5fc8aa507bc",
+      "statement": "CertificateFlow.Sign parses not-before/not-after and template data, posts the api.SignRequest (CSR, OTT, validity, TemplateData) via client.Sign, and writes the returned certificate chain as PEM with fileutil.WriteFile mode 0600.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L249-L293",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68d184fe51e4b0f03644cfc19e943e946724961c1a684e36d1cf5b5fb87e1aae:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5d66eac5faaf41089ad80fb60c9f2cac",
+      "statement": "GetClient trusts the CA via ca.WithRootSHA256 when the token carries a sha claim and an http(s) audience (defaulting the CA URL to the audience), otherwise requires --ca-url and a root file (defaulting to $STEPPATH/certs/root_ca.crt); in offline mode it returns the offline CA directly.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L134-L171",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eac06e54a30b1c44b73cef0ba05ec80a593dabe45011372e61bc7bd15ba6eeb7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ba948850d8094aaf9cf7f10dd5d6f99e",
+      "statement": "step ca sign reads a CSR file, requires --token (incompatible with --offline), and for OIDC, AWS, GCP, Azure, and K8sSA tokens verifies that the token subject matches the CSR CommonName before calling flow.Sign.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/sign.go#L150-L217",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:933a5682687525f1184ec156c0fefc93970474632da7d5185b3fdf31e2b420e7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_fdef2be1c71b4b92879ff6eebc662092",
+      "statement": "NewOfflineCA parses the CA configuration from --ca-config, injects the --password-file contents into the config, requires at least one provisioner, and builds an in-process authority.Authority; it is a process-wide singleton to avoid double initialization failures such as badger database locks.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L28-L80",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b93b34801a087cc316ec780e023f135f33741c48eecbcfc12146485e1384010f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e7264c2c86de43f2bcc732f2b30de58b",
+      "statement": "The OfflineCA derives audiences from the config's first DNS name (https://<host>/sign, /revoke, /ssh/sign, /ssh/renew, /ssh/revoke, /ssh/rekey, /renew), returns GetCaURL as https://<first DNS name>, and exposes VerifyClientCert against its own root and intermediate pools.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L81-L171",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5c9966d27444629d01802ace7ba4e5fc422664b1b92cee6baafc32051a086d0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_02cc92e4c9b04473ba111a9504833e21",
+      "statement": "The ACME issuance flow lives in utils/cautils/acme_flow.go and uses the ACME-specific flags defined in command/ca/ca.go (--acme directory URL, --contact, --http-listen, EAB key id/reference).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/ca.go#L42-L61",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:05f0425433a477b3f1f79a9315440c5931022ce2fcf0d7f2845bba7c2dc281a9:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acme_flow.go",
+          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:36110e9c5d1fd5f4d4e3f2c9435842cb70078a40325cd3fb2c691d3575679351"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-08-31T08:02:07.014Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/integrations/ca-client.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/integrations/ca-client.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/integrations/ca-client.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:44bb63e17d60e0ed3d5afdbb4b0255d31d60a98ef9225107a011706197dd3aa0",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8197d8fac76a4d99ac78e36118d4c18e",
+      "statement": "The CaClient interface defines Sign, Renew, RenewWithToken, Revoke, Rekey, the SSH operations (SSHSign, SSHRenew, SSHRekey, SSHRevoke, SSHRoots, SSHFederation, SSHConfig, SSHCheckHost, SSHGetHosts, SSHBastion), Version, GetRootCAs, and GetCaURL, letting command actions serve both online and offline modes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L27-L48",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d9082e3dc6bfd7f7ef4fda03bbc2077610af0366eb8e8085ee0b4043dd65958:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_deeb7a1618b14fc1abb782193aa8411b",
+      "statement": "cautils.NewClient returns the offline CA when --offline is set (--ca-config then required), otherwise builds ca.NewClient from flags.ParseCaURL and --root, defaulting the root to $STEPPATH/certs/root_ca.crt and erroring with a required-flag error when neither exists.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L50-L74",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5be85b9610de8b89ff776d3d358f4d248715195dbbb66e6ec002335f566e2eb2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f83a98395d2e46b581453fb520fc728c",
+      "statement": "NewOfflineCA parses the CA configuration JSON, requires at least one provisioner, merges --password-file into the config, and initializes an in-process authority.Authority; a package-level offlineInstance singleton is returned on subsequent calls because double initialization can fail on locks (badger is the comment's example).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L42-L80",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1ce1f863a65a8ab791c61be14a9a880172f47c6ec634cb21498f9df5ab0c25a9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_246b953d840847bc8706ec95902737d7",
+      "statement": "OfflineCA synthesizes URLs rather than dialing: CaURL/GetCaURL is https://<config.DNSNames[0]>, audiences use the same per-token-type paths, and GetRootCAs always returns nil.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L141-L171",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e9d5a53a63c64b355a80a456292b7bb89a651cd3f8754b1315f96c9656c71568:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L81-L92",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf854f5557fe675122d829cc20f4f17295efe60476352a66198cd3018639295a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6027c199701841caaabed4022fc07169",
+      "statement": "OfflineCA implements Sign, Renew (extracting the peer certificate from the caller's http.Transport), RenewWithToken (AuthorizeRenewToken then authority.Renew), Revoke, and Rekey by calling authority methods and re-wrapping results into the api response shapes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L196-L343",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e28484b99afddc7d40605051a5d7c2872754f40a4cc9843ee9148535f053386f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6a03f4b808084812a945dd7fc485fd2c",
+      "statement": "OfflineCA exposes Provisioners() for offline token generation and VerifyClientCert, which validates a certificate/key pair and verifies the chain against the offline root and intermediate pools.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L171-L173",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:54114e74036bd4c495035293eee0b4c83d2b96ca1576c49130463f1bf2cf4a1d:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L96-L139",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b10d394c73dd23601bc131b91da799136adaf4e08ebc1b3837c7f6858d98780:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8e4d1cc6491f493a9f34500c1ad5c74e",
+      "statement": "NewUnauthenticatedAdminClient requires --ca-url (no offline variant) and a root with the same default, and returns an unauthenticated ca.AdminClient for the management API.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L76-L96",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a27e860b31e6ccd1a826a323b2596956f0154999b0158e441c22e0b847df5a2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d3516444140447d9a2ddf0d95e436356",
+      "statement": "NewAdminClient authenticates with --admin-cert/--admin-key (each requiring the other) via ca.WithAdminX5C; without them it prompts for the admin subject (or --admin-subject), generates a key, obtains a sign token via NewTokenFlow, signs a CSR, and uses the issued chain as the X5C admin credential, parameterized by --admin-provisioner and --admin-password-file.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L98-L204",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6b12568c1887e4616cdb405132aee3899ecc9493cd61d3c2d4ea9609b7af81f0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-08-31T08:02:07.014Z"
+  }
+}

